# Session discipline

- One bounded slice per chat. Prefer new chat over expanding an old one.
- Reject broad prompts ("implement long mode", "add Windows support"). Split them.
- Start in Plan Mode: files to touch + acceptance tests. Edit only after that plan is clear.
- Prefer invoking project skills: `next-slice`, `implement-instruction`, `implement-device`, `guest-boot-debug`, `quality-gate`.
- Do not let two agents edit CPU state layout or instruction metadata at the same time; use worktrees.

# Prompt shape (required)

```text
Task: <one feature>
In scope: <bullets>
Out of scope: <bullets>
Acceptance tests: <bullets>
Spec refs: <manual sections or docs paths>
```

# Stop conditions

- Stop when the slice's acceptance tests pass and `quality-gate` is green.
- Stop and ask if a change requires redesigning crate boundaries, CPU state, or metadata schema.
- Never continue into the next epic without an explicit user request.
